WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:14.818
Three points in the complex plane
There are three points in the complex plane. A has coordinate one plus i, B
has three plus i, and C has one plus three i.

2
00:00:14.818 --> 00:00:27.364
Calculate vector AB
To study the triangle from A, calculate the complex coordinate of vector AB.
Subtract A's coordinate from B's to obtain two.

3
00:00:27.364 --> 00:00:39.455
Calculate vector AC
Likewise, the complex coordinate of vector AC is C's coordinate minus A's. The
real parts cancel and two i remains.

4
00:00:39.455 --> 00:00:51.091
Compare the vectors
Now divide two i by two. The quotient is i. The denominator is nonzero, so
this division is valid.

5
00:00:51.091 --> 00:01:06.818
A right angle and equal lengths
The number i has argument pi over two and modulus one. The angle between the
vectors is therefore a right angle, and their lengths from A are equal.

6
00:01:06.818 --> 00:01:20.727
A right isosceles triangle at A
The triangle ABC is right-angled and isosceles at A. The calculation
established both the angle and the lengths, rather than relying on the sketch.
